# Cloudflare Pages response headers for duck-sounds.
#
# SCOPED TO /phonebench/, DELIBERATELY. The first draft of this file put
# `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` on `/*`, which would have changed
# the headers the live walk demo is served under — and COEP is not a cosmetic
# header: under require-corp every subresource that does not opt in stops
# loading, with no error the page can show. The probe needs isolation; the demo
# did not ask for it and is not part of this change.
#
# WHY THE PROBE WANTS ISOLATION AT ALL. The single-threaded MuJoCo build this
# runs needs none of it. The probe MEASURES whether `SharedArrayBuffer` exists
# and whether `crossOriginIsolated` is true, and a page that never sent these
# headers would be measuring its own omission rather than the browser. With
# them set, a `false` reading on an iPhone is Safari's answer and not ours.

/phonebench/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Pages serves an unknown extension as application/octet-stream, and
# `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` refuses anything that is not
# `application/wasm`. The symptom is one console line about an incorrect
# response MIME type and an otherwise blank page.
/phonebench/assets/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
